WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.577 --> 00:00:15.278
Jason sat in the farmyard playing a video game.

2
00:00:17.238 --> 00:00:19.399
Suddenly someone bumped into his arm.

3
00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.801
"Ugh!" Jason cried.

4
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.842
"You just made me lose!"

5
00:00:27.523 --> 00:00:28.763
He turned to see a goat.

6
00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:30.484
Nina laughed.

7
00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:34.537
"The goat wants to play a video game too!"

8
00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:37.518
Chef came outside.

9
00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:42.300
"The peaches are ripe, so we'll make peach cookies today.

10
00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:44.141
Let's pick some first."

11
00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:48.643
The kids followed Chef to the peach trees.

12
00:00:50.424 --> 00:00:53.085
They began picking peaches and putting them in baskets.

13
00:00:54.786 --> 00:00:57.567
"I love peaches," Izzie said.

14
00:00:57.587 --> 00:00:58.928
"Me too."

15
00:01:00.052 --> 00:01:02.313
Jason climbed a ladder to reach the branches.

16
00:01:04.113 --> 00:01:06.594
With his hands full, he started to come down.

17
00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.695
But a goat was blocking him.

18
00:01:09.715 --> 00:01:11.755
"Move it!"

19
00:01:12.135 --> 00:01:12.916
Jason said.

20
00:01:13.616 --> 00:01:14.476
Bobby laughed.

21
00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:18.777
"Those goats are troublemakers!"

22
00:01:20.658 --> 00:01:21.998
Nina looked at the baskets.

23
00:01:22.018 --> 00:01:25.879
"Do we need all of these peaches for the cookies?"

24
00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:28.040
"No," Chef said.

25
00:01:28.844 --> 00:01:30.906
"But I'll sell some at my farmstand tomorrow."

26
00:01:33.228 --> 00:01:35.770
In the kitchen everyone read the cookie recipe.

27
00:01:36.951 --> 00:01:40.593
"Jason and Izzie, please peel and chop the peaches," Chef said.

28
00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:43.175
"Bobby, take care of the butter mixture.

29
00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:46.398
Nina, you can whisk the dry ingredients."

30
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.500
Everyone got to work.

31
00:01:51.182 --> 00:01:53.744
Bobby mixed brown sugar and white sugar with butter.

32
00:01:56.428 --> 00:01:58.930
Then he added the egg, vanilla, and lemon juice.

33
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.095
"Ready for the dry ingredients!"

34
00:02:05.276 --> 00:02:08.338
Nina was still whisking the flour, salt, and baking soda.

35
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.822
She put in cinnamon and nutmeg.

36
00:02:14.844 --> 00:02:17.185
Then she added the mixture to Bobby's bowl.

37
00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:20.608
"Here come the peaches!"

38
00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.632
Jason stirred everything together.

39
00:02:26.376 --> 00:02:29.499
Chef lined a baking sheet with parchment paper and greased it.

40
00:02:31.861 --> 00:02:35.183
Izzie began dropping tablespoons of dough onto the baking sheet.

41
00:02:35.203 --> 00:02:39.487
"Keep them about five centimeters apart," Chef said.

42
00:02:39.507 --> 00:02:42.809
"Otherwise they'll clump together when they bake."

43
00:02:49.014 --> 00:02:50.916
Chef put the baking sheet in the oven.

44
00:02:52.668 --> 00:02:58.092
"Bake for 14 minutes at 175 degrees Celsius," Izzie said.

45
00:02:58.112 --> 00:03:02.876
"Hmm. We do have a lot of peaches," Chef said.

46
00:03:02.896 --> 00:03:04.817
"Let's make a few more batches."

47
00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:09.441
While the cookies baked, the kids washed the dishes.

48
00:03:09.461 --> 00:03:13.644
"We made a lot of cookies," Nina said.

49
00:03:13.664 --> 00:03:16.486
"You can take some home," Chef said.

50
00:03:16.506 --> 00:03:19.188
"We'll keep the rest here as snacks."

51
00:03:21.484 --> 00:03:23.526
The next day the kids were in the garden.

52
00:03:24.807 --> 00:03:27.409
They were picking vegetables to sell at the farmstand.

53
00:03:27.429 --> 00:03:31.032
"My family loved those peach cookies!"

54
00:03:31.372 --> 00:03:32.072
Bobby said.

55
00:03:32.092 --> 00:03:36.516
"I'm glad there are so many left over," Izzie said.

56
00:03:37.877 --> 00:03:39.758
Soon the baskets were full of vegetables.

57
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.782
The kids carried the baskets back to the farmyard.

58
00:03:44.882 --> 00:03:46.404
Chef was bringing out the peaches.

59
00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:50.657
"A customer!"

60
00:03:51.017 --> 00:03:52.718
Izzie said, pointing to a car.

61
00:03:52.738 --> 00:03:54.599
"Oh no!

62
00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:55.780
We're not ready yet!"

63
00:03:56.941 --> 00:03:58.461
Chef looked around in a panic.

64
00:03:58.481 --> 00:04:03.084
"Kids, please grab the signs and the cashbox.

65
00:04:04.005 --> 00:04:04.625
They're inside."

66
00:04:06.106 --> 00:04:07.767
He jogged toward the farmstand.

67
00:04:10.288 --> 00:04:12.150
The kids carried the things to the stand.

68
00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.612
Then they went back to get the peaches and vegetables.

69
00:04:19.456 --> 00:04:20.337
"Uh-oh!" Nina shouted.

70
00:04:21.738 --> 00:04:22.639
Izzie gasped.

71
00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.762
"The goats made a mess.

72
00:04:26.863 --> 00:04:28.825
And they're eating everything!"

73
00:04:28.845 --> 00:04:32.388
"I knew they were troublemakers!"

74
00:04:32.788 --> 00:04:33.529
Bobby said.

75
00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:35.911
Chef groaned.

76
00:04:35.931 --> 00:04:37.332
"Now what?

77
00:04:38.173 --> 00:04:39.514
We don't have much to sell."

78
00:04:40.895 --> 00:04:42.096
Jason looked at the goats.

79
00:04:42.116 --> 00:04:45.860
"I have an idea, but we need a new sign!"

80
00:04:50.696 --> 00:04:52.918
Later the kids closed the farmstand.

81
00:04:54.799 --> 00:04:55.960
Chef turned to Jason.

82
00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.462
"Selling the leftover peach cookies was a great idea.

83
00:05:00.463 --> 00:05:02.284
Everyone loved feeding the goats too!

84
00:05:02.984 --> 00:05:03.745
Thank you, Jason."

85
00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:06.507
Jason gave a goat a cucumber.

86
00:05:06.527 --> 00:05:08.108
"Glad I could help!"
